        "original_id": "52f29d62-bdd4-526e-b02a-2fb93d83930d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Robert Marks III, Andrew D. Gillum\n- Places: Tallahassee, Florida\n- Roles: Mayor, city commissioner, lawyer, politician\n\nFacts:\n- John Robert Marks III was born on July 25, 1947.\n- Andrew D. Gillum was born on July 26, 1979.\n- In February 2003, John Robert Marks III began serving as Mayor of Tallahassee, Florida.\n- In February 2003, at age 23, Andrew D. Gillum became the youngest person ever elected to the Tallahassee City Commission.\n- John Robert Marks III served as Mayor of Tallahassee, Florida until November 2014.\n- On November 21, 2014, Andrew D. Gillum succeeded John Robert Marks III as Mayor of Tallahassee, Florida.\n- John Robert Marks III is an American lawyer and politician.\n- Andrew D. Gillum is an American politician who serves as mayor and formerly served as a city commissioner of Tallahassee, Florida.",
